    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. \n\nThe change is complete. I implemented the `initials` derived field:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` JSON response.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` and an `initials(Owner)` helper that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"john\"` + `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`). It null-guards each name so a missing part is simply omitted.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
